unenroll: '--not-a-declared-flag' is not a flag unenroll declares. Declared: --dry-run, --force, --help, --home, --instants-dir, --porcelain, --slot. Refused, not ignored: a parser that accepts what no spec declares is a second, hand-maintained copy of the flag list.
fleet unenroll --slot <value>
    take a slot out of the pool
    --slot <value>               (required) the slot name
    --force                      unenroll a slot that is currently leased, stranding that work
    --home <value>               the record/pool store root; overrides $FLEET_HOME
    --instants-dir <value>       where instants live; overrides $FLEET_INSTANTS
    --porcelain                  machine form on stdout: tab-separated, no banner (NFR2-7)
    --help                       print this verb's derived usage and exit 0
    --dry-run                    evaluate every gate and CREATE NOTHING; the delta is asserted to be zero

exit codes:
    0  ok
    1  needs attention / check failed
    2  bad input
    3  no capacity
    4  refused by an admission rule
    pane-guard only (FD-10):
    0  safe
    10 queued-text
    11 mid-turn
    12 not-claude
    13 unknown-pane

